## 12. Recommendation Status and Follow-Up

Each recommendation must have a status:

- Active.
- Acknowledged.
- Action In Progress.
- Completed.
- Escalated.
- Resolved.

Phase 5 must use updates from Phase 3 and Phase 4 to maintain recommendation status.

- If Phase 3 continues reporting the same ongoing finding, update the existing recommendation instead of creating duplicates.
- If Phase 3 reports that the concern has improved or is no longer present, update the recommendation appropriately.
- If Phase 3 increases the risk classification, update the recommendation severity and escalation requirement.
- Do not mark a recommendation as resolved only because the astronaut acknowledged it.
- Preserve the full recommendation history when a recommendation changes level or status.
- Keep the original Phase 3 analytical finding ID and Phase 4 alert ID associated with each recommendation.

